::recipe
conversion stage: initial

name: Fall Vegetable and Chickpea Curry
source: https://publicdomainrecipes.com/fall-vegetable-and-chickpea-curry/
source author: joel-maxuel
source license: Public domain (Unlicense)
ingredients: US
units: US
category: soup/stew
tags: curry, chickpeas, vegetables
dietary: vegetarian
serves: 4
active time: ~15m
total time: ~40m
image: fall-vegetable-and-chickpea-curry.webp

::ingredients

(butter) 1tbsp
(onion, chopped) 1
(Thai red curry paste) 2tbsp
(ginger, minced) 1tbsp
(sweet potato, large, peeled, 1/2in chunks) 1
(zucchini, small, 1/2in chunks) 1
(red pepper, 1/2in pieces) 1
(chickpeas, canned, rinsed, drained) 28oz
(lime) 1
(flour; wheat) 3tbsp
(milk) 1 1/2 cups
(coriander, fresh, chopped) 1/2 cup
(water) 1/2 cup
(salt) to taste
(yogurt, optional, for serving) as desired

::equipment

(frying pan, large, non-stick)

::instructions

(butter) <heat, frying pan, medium-high heat>
    + (onion)
    <cook, stirring, 2m>
    + (Thai red curry paste)
    + (ginger)
    <cook, stirring, 1m>

{curry} =
    (sweet potato) +
    (zucchini) +
    (red pepper) +
    (salt) +
    (water)

{curry} <cook, covered, stirring occasionally, ~10m, until vegetables soften>
    + (chickpeas)
    + (lime: zest)
    + (lime: juice)
    <cook, stirring frequently, ~5m, until vegetables are tender and liquid evaporates>

{slurry} =
    (flour) +
    (milk)

{slurry} <whisk>

{curry} + {slurry}
    <stir in, gradually>
    <bring to simmer>
    <simmer, medium heat, stirring occasionally, 5m>
    + (coriander)
    <stir>

Optional [
    {curry} + (yogurt) <serve with>
]

::notes
The source suggests serving this curry over rice or on its own with a dollop of yogurt.